                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "(Review In Construction)\n\n+2010 iPhone game that helped usher in a wave of next-gen full quality games to mobile phones. \n-Too Tedious random clicking forever to get lucky creating a new Element.\n-Not enough of a hint to solve the Element equation.\n-Non-logical recipes for a lot of the Elements, making the experience a click-all-athon.\n-After spending hours random clicking to create the requested element, fed-up i started googling the craft recipe, which is cheating, and i don't like to cheat in games, but the game is poorly designed to not respect the User's time.\n-The Hint Button lied for the recipe of Pyramid of Cheops (said Stone+Human+Stone.  But the real one was Sand+Corpse+Stone)\n+/- Good game for ages 7-14.\n+Decent music.\n+More content then expected, lots of different game modes & achievement unlocks.\n-Overpriced.\n-Sometimes the game asks you to craft elements that you have already crafted, which is annoying.\n\nA game i thought id enjoy, but didn't because of how tedious the random clicking to get lucky is.\nWhich means, i wouldn't recommend it to any of my friends.\nGame is worth $1-2, and now they have 90% off sales for the series.  If you're curious about trying it out just wait for that big sale.  Game had potential, but more hints were needed to make it an enjoyable experience and less of a click-a-thon.\n\n2/5 Stars",
